<item rdf:about='http://www.makumba.org/page/OptionTagAttributeValueAttributeComments'><title>OptionTagAttributeValueAttributeComments</title><link>http://www.makumba.org/page/OptionTagAttributeValueAttributeComments</link><description>Cristian Bogdan changed this page on Tue Apr 05 00:39:06 CEST 2016:&lt;br /&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;table class="diff" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0"&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="diff"&gt;At line 1 changed one line&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="diffrem"&gt;If not indicated, nil (null option) is default&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="diffadd"&gt;If not indicated, nil (null option) is default. null option can be also marked as &amp;quot;nil&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;&amp;quot; (except for char types, where it is a valid option)&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;</description><wiki:version>3</wiki:version><wiki:diff>http://www.makumba.org/page/OptionTagAttributeValueAttributeComments?do=Diff&amp;r1=-1</wiki:diff><dc:date>2016-04-04T22:39:06Z</dc:date><dc:creator>Cristian Bogdan</dc:creator><wiki:history>http://www.makumba.org/page/OptionTagAttributeValueAttributeComments?do=PageInfo</wiki:history></item>
<item rdf:about='http://www.makumba.org/page/QueryLanguages'><title>QueryLanguages</title><link>http://www.makumba.org/page/QueryLanguages</link><description>Cristian Bogdan changed this page on Mon Apr 04 23:46:25 CEST 2016:&lt;br /&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;table class="diff" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0"&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="diff"&gt;At line 78 changed one line&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="diffrem"&gt;Makumba automatically creates the SQL statements from the (Object) Query Languages MQL or HQL. Doing so, it converts elements such as %%prettify label.subTable %% to corresponding JOINs in SQL. Normally, Makumba will create default (inner) JOINs between tables. However, if the expression contains two or more &amp;quot;.&amp;quot;, then all but the last &amp;quot;.&amp;quot; will translate to a LEFT JOIN.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="diffadd"&gt;Makumba automatically creates the SQL statements from the (Object) Query Languages MQL or HQL. Doing so, it converts elements such as %%prettify label.subTable %% to corresponding JOINs in SQL. Normally, Makumba will create default (inner) JOINs between tables. However, if the expression (label.pointerField.field) goes via a nullable pointerField, a LEFT JOIN is generated. This is the default behaviour, but can be suppressed by specifying the join type explicitly.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;</description><wiki:version>7</wiki:version><wiki:diff>http://www.makumba.org/page/QueryLanguages?do=Diff&amp;r1=-1</wiki:diff><dc:date>2016-04-04T21:46:25Z</dc:date><dc:creator>Cristian Bogdan</dc:creator><wiki:history>http://www.makumba.org/page/QueryLanguages?do=PageInfo</wiki:history></item>
