<item rdf:about='http://www.makumba.org/page/Plugin'><title>Plugin</title><link>http://www.makumba.org/page/Plugin</link><description>Filip Kis changed this page on Sat Jul 23 10:55:26 CEST 2011:&lt;br /&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;table class="diff" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0"&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="diff"&gt;At line 12 changed one line&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="diffrem"&gt;__Requirment:__ Eclipse J2EE Helios (3.6) or higher. You can find it on [Eclipse Download Site|http://www.eclipse.org/downloads/]&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="diffadd"&gt;__Requirment:__ Eclipse J2EE Helios (3.6.x). You can find it on [Eclipse Download Site|http://www.eclipse.org/helios/]. The newest Eclipse version (Indigo) is not yet supported. Stay tuned for updates.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;</description><wiki:version>11</wiki:version><wiki:diff>http://www.makumba.org/page/Plugin?do=Diff&amp;r1=-1</wiki:diff><dc:date>2011-07-23T08:55:26Z</dc:date><dc:creator>Filip Kis</dc:creator><wiki:history>http://www.makumba.org/page/Plugin?do=PageInfo</wiki:history></item>
<item rdf:about='http://www.makumba.org/page/MakumbaManifesto'><title>MakumbaManifesto</title><link>http://www.makumba.org/page/MakumbaManifesto</link><description>Cristian Bogdan changed this page on Sat Apr 09 08:05:06 CEST 2011:&lt;br /&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;table class="diff" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0"&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="diff"&gt;At line 9 changed one line&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="diffrem"&gt;We also recognize that the way data is viewed is often very similar with the way data is described in the data model.  By allowing for queries in views, and by avoiding the repeating of the data description we advocate a smaller separation between data description and its user interface view, therefore weakening the model-view separation. While we do respect the MVC in general, we believe that it the strong separations it enforces are often not needed in applications dominated by browsing and updating, and we argue for the use of strong separation only when the situation demands it.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="diffadd"&gt;By allowing for queries in views, and by avoiding the repeating of the data description in the model-view communication we advocate a smaller separation between data description and its user interface view, therefore weakening the model-view separation. While we do respect the MVC in general, we believe that it the strong separations it enforces are often not needed in applications dominated by browsing and updating, and we argue for the use of strong separation only when the situation demands it.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;</description><wiki:version>4</wiki:version><wiki:diff>http://www.makumba.org/page/MakumbaManifesto?do=Diff&amp;r1=-1</wiki:diff><dc:date>2011-04-09T06:05:06Z</dc:date><dc:creator>Cristian Bogdan</dc:creator><wiki:history>http://www.makumba.org/page/MakumbaManifesto?do=PageInfo</wiki:history></item>
<item rdf:about='http://www.makumba.org/page/Main'><title>Main</title><link>http://www.makumba.org/page/Main</link><description>Cristian Bogdan changed this page on Sat Apr 09 07:43:46 CEST 2011:&lt;br /&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;table class="diff" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0"&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="diff"&gt;At line 11 changed one line&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="diffrem"&gt;* __everything is a query-fragment__. Displaying and modifying data is made simple especially through powerful features such as the Makumba lists and Makumba forms.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="diffadd"&gt;* __everything is a query-fragment__. A large part of the application code can be expressed in queries and query fragments: displaying and modifying data, authentication, authorization, etc.&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="diff"&gt;At line 13 changed one line&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="diffrem"&gt;* __mixing Model and View via queries __ is beneficial for web application development and helps eliminate many application layers without much architectural penalty, and leads to intuitive code. See Manifesto&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="diffadd"&gt;* __mixing Model and View via queries __ is beneficial for web application development and helps eliminate many application layers without much architectural penalty, and leads to intuitive code. See [Manifesto|MakumbaManifesto].&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;</description><wiki:version>8</wiki:version><wiki:diff>http://www.makumba.org/page/Main?do=Diff&amp;r1=-1</wiki:diff><dc:date>2011-04-09T05:43:46Z</dc:date><dc:creator>Cristian Bogdan</dc:creator><wiki:history>http://www.makumba.org/page/Main?do=PageInfo</wiki:history></item>
